  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 18. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 回数 — 同じことを何回したかという数。\n2. 回想 — 昔のことを思い出すこと。\n3. 改造 — 作りを変えて別の働きなどを加えること。\n4. 買い出し — 必要な品物をまとめて買いに行くこと。\n5. 改築 — 建物の一部や全体を建て直すこと。\n6. 懐中電灯 — 手に持って使う電池式の明かり。\n7. 開通 — 道路や鉄道などが通れるようになること。\n8. 買い手 — 品物などを買う人。\n9. 解読 — 読みにくい文字や暗号などの意味を読み取ること。\n10. 飼い主 — 動物を飼っている人。\n11. 開発 — 新しい物や技術などを作り出すこと。\n12. 開発者 — 新しい製品や仕組みなどを作る人。\n13. 開封 — 封をしてある袋や手紙などを開けること。\n14. 回復 — 弱ったり悪くなったりした状態から元に戻ること。\n15. 開閉 — 開けることと閉めること。\n16. 開幕 — 舞台や大会などが始まること。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
